wire：
    directional：方向特性，这是物理上没有的
        Unlike physical wires, wires (and other signals) in Verilog are directional；
        only one direction, from (usually one) source to the sinks；

    continuous assignment：连续赋值
        verilog中的概念
        In a Verilog "continuous assignment" (assign left_side = right_side;), 
        the value of the signal on the right side is driven onto the wire on the left side;
        continuous:
            the assignment continues all the time even if the right side's value changes;
            有改变立即传递特性；

        the order in which they appear in the code does not matter:
            Unlike a programming language, assign statements ("continuous assignments") describe connections between things, not the action of copying a value from one thing to another.

常见运算符：
NOT gate：
    implement an inverter；

AND gate:
    implements an AND gate;
    a wire that has no drivers will have an undefined value (often treated as 0 when synthesizing hardware). 没有驱动的input信号如何被处理；

Nor Gate:或非
    A NOR gate is an OR gate with its output inverted；not or;
    A NOR function needs two operators when written in Verilog.
    只能输入都为0时，才输出1；

Xnor Gate：同或
    输入相同时，输出1；



声明wire信号：
    在module中，声明wire类型的信号；
    As circuits become more complex, you will need wires to connect internal components together；
    When you need to use a wire, you should declare it in the body of the module, somewhere before it is first used,原则：使用前声明；



7458: 小芯片
    The 7458 is a chip with four AND gates and two OR gates；
    提供了电路图结构，需要用verilog写出来；





